{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/196902-simple-social-rolls-instead-of-social-maneuvering","id":196902,"title":"Simple Social Rolls instead of Social Maneuvering","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-14T09:57:28-07:00","id":196902,"title":"Simple Social Rolls instead of Social Maneuvering","content":"In what situations can I call for traditional resisted or contested social rolls instead of the new Social Mechanics roll? Sometimes it seems like an instant action would be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T13:40:58-07:00","id":198189,"title":"","content":"Just slightly the wrong forum for this question since the mechanics are part of the GMC-era systems update as a whole, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Those times where it seems more appropriate to put the action down to a single instant roll-off are generally the times where you're encouraged to do so. Social Maneuvering is more for things you'd have to talk somebody around to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T21:22:53-07:00","id":198544,"title":"","content":"Personally, I always use social maneuvering, but in situations where it would be more appropriate to just make a single roll and keep the flow of play moving, I will either max out the impression or use forcing doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T21:41:10-07:00","id":198551,"title":"","content":"And if you're still feeling uncomfortable with using Social Maneuvering like either of the excellent suggestions above, you can always just make it an extended action with a required number of successes equal to what would've been the Doors. Or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:07:05-07:00","id":198956,"title":"","content":"I like the mechanic just fine. Maybe it's analogous to detailed combat vs down and dirty combat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""